CORRECTION appended 2026-08-05T07:38:42Z — THE COVERAGE TABLE ABOVE IS WRONG.

fuzz.sh selected the wrong instrumented binary (a cached -Donly="fuzz csv"
triage build), so the PCs above resolved against a mismatched PC table and every
module reported a fraction of its true size — 'window NOT ENTERED 0/138' when
the truth is 215/376. The runs/unique-runs/PCs-covered lines are read from the
coverage map header, not the binary, so THOSE are correct.

Root cause + fix: fuzz.sh now picks the binary that maximizes 'attributed'
(project-file PCs) instead of using a timestamp heuristic; covreport prints that
number as the audit trail. 'unresolved' does not discriminate (316 vs 323).

